# No co-authoring text in commits

When creating or amending git commits, do **not** add any co-authoring text to the commit message.

Forbidden examples:

- `Co-authored-by: …`
- `Co-Authored-By: …`
- Cursor / Copilot / AI “Generated with …” trailers
- Any similar trailer that attributes the commit to another author or tool

Commit messages must contain only the intended title and body from the user or the drafted suggestion — nothing else appended.
